# Frame and overlays: Layer orders what is painted on top, with negative layers beneath the content in flow.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Layer
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: square
			Box:
				Width: 110
				Height: 70
				Padding: 6 8
				Border: 1
				Border color: accent
				Background: #FFFFFF
			Typography:
				Size: 8.5
				Line height: 11
	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Layer
		Paragraph: Positioned boxes are painted after the flow, in document order. `Layer` changes that order: higher layers go on top, and a negative layer goes beneath the content in flow. Without `Layer`, a box counts as `Layer: 0`.
			Style: intro
		Text: Without Layer: the later box covers the earlier one
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 20 auto auto 20
				Text: First
					Style: square
			Overlay:
				Offset: 45 auto auto 80
				Text: Second
					Style: square
			Overlay:
				Offset: 70 auto auto 140
				Text: Third
					Style: square
		Text: Layer: 3, 2 and 1: the first box on top
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 20 auto auto 20
				Layer: 3
				Text: First, Layer: 3
					Style: square
			Overlay:
				Offset: 45 auto auto 80
				Layer: 2
				Text: Second, Layer: 2
					Style: square
			Overlay:
				Offset: 70 auto auto 140
				Layer: 1
				Text: Third, Layer: 1
					Style: square
		Text: Layer: -1 beneath the text of the Frame
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 0 auto 0 0
				Layer: -1
				Block:
					Box:
						Width: 160
						Height: 100%
						Background: sand
			Paragraph: This paragraph is in the flow of the Frame. The sand band is an Overlay with Layer: -1, so it is painted beneath the paragraph and not over it.
				Box:
					Padding: 10
